{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/ios"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"SwiftGodot"}],"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","title":"iOS Platform Integration"},"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot"]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Converting a Viewport into an Image","type":"heading","anchor":"Converting-a-Viewport-into-an-Image","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you happen to have a viewport, you can create a screenshot of it like this:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["func getImage (from: SceneTree) -> SwiftGodot.Image? {","\tfrom.root?.getViewport()?.getTexture()?.getImage()","}"]},{"level":2,"text":"Converting a SwiftGodot.image into a UIImage","type":"heading","anchor":"Converting-a-SwiftGodotimage-into-a-UIImage"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This function will attempt to convert a SwiftGodot image into a UIImage:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["extension SwiftGodot.Image {","    func toUIImage() -> UIImage? {","        let width = Int(getWidth())","        let height = Int(getHeight())","        ","        \/\/ Ensure the image format is compatible (RGBA8)","        if getFormat() != Image.Format.rgba8 {","            convert(format: Image.Format.rgba8)","        }","        ","        guard let pixelData = getData().asData() else { return nil }","        ","        let colorSpace = CGColorSpaceCreateDeviceRGB()","        let bitmapInfo = CGBitmapInfo(rawValue: CGImageAlphaInfo.premultipliedLast.rawValue)","        ","        guard let provider = CGDataProvider(data: pixelData as CFData) else { return nil }","        ","        guard let cgImage = CGImage(","            width: width,","            height: height,","            bitsPerComponent: 8,","            bitsPerPixel: 32,","            bytesPerRow: width * 4,","            space: colorSpace,","            bitmapInfo: bitmapInfo,","            provider: provider,","            decode: nil,","            shouldInterpolate: false,","            intent: .defaultIntent","        ) else { return nil }","        ","        return UIImage(cgImage: cgImage)","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"},{"anchor":"Converting-a-SwiftGodotColor-into-a-SwiftUIColor","text":"Converting a SwiftGodot.Color into a SwiftUI.Color","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"code":["extension SwiftGodot.Color {","    \/\/\/ Creates a SwiftUI.Color from a SwiftGodot.Color","    public func asSwiftUI() -> SwiftUI.Color {","        SwiftUI.Color(","            red: Double(red),","            green: Double(green),","            blue: Double(blue),","            opacity: Double(alpha)","        )","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Converting-PackedByteArray-into-a-Swift-Data","text":"Converting PackedByteArray into a Swift Data"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["extension PackedByteArray {","    public func asData() -> Data? {","        return withUnsafeAccessToData { ptr, count in Data (bytes: ptr, count: count) }","    }","}"]},{"level":3,"text":"Making GodotError conform to LocalizedError","anchor":"Making-GodotError-conform-to-LocalizedError","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is convenient if you want to easily bubble up GodotError messages in"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"codeListing","code":["","\/\/ The @retroactive is to avoid the warning on LocalizedError, which is not on SwiftGodot,","\/\/ because SwiftGodot avoids taking a dependency on Foundation","extension GodotError: @retroactive LocalizedError {","    public var failureReason: String? {","        return localizedDescription","    }","    public var errorDescription: String? {","        return localizedDescription","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This page contains some examples of code that might be useful to combine Godot"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"with iOS APIs.","type":"text"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Windows"],"anchor":"Platform-Integration","title":"Platform Integration","generated":true}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/iOS","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot":{"role":"collection","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot","url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot","title":"SwiftGodot","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Framework to write Godot Game Extensions using the Swift Programming Language.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://SwiftGodot/documentation/SwiftGodot/Windows":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftGodot\/documentation\/SwiftGodot\/Windows","type":"topic","title":"Using SwiftGodot on Windows","role":"article","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/swiftgodot\/windows"}}}